        "node::W2889241664",
        "node::W2992155721"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline Hf-Mo-Ta-Ti-Zr alloy has coarse grains.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline alloy has a density of approximately 12-13 g/cm³.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Severe plastic deformation followed by partial recrystallization can produce a heterogeneous grain structure.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "node::W2992155721"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting heterogeneous structure will contain a mixture of ultrafine and coarse grains or a grain-size gradient.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "node::W2992155721"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strain gradients between coarse and fine regions generate back-stress strengthening.",
